const welcomeSections=[
  ['internet','Internet','⌁','<strong>WIFI: user:</strong> Upstairs<br><strong>Passcode:</strong> thiya7fo'],
  ['water','Water','◌','Our water is supplied by an onsite well, so we are not connected to the mains. It is a natural hard-water area and a water softener is installed. The water is safe to drink, although it may taste a little different to water you are used to.'],
  ['waste','Waste','♻','There are two large bins in the kitchen for black-bin and green-bin waste, plus a small brown bin. Please remove all waste at check-out and use the waste-management area just outside the estate, at the top of the road on the right.'],
  ['heating','Heating & cooling','♨','Heating is set to 19°C for your arrival. Adjust it using the Nest thermostat in the superking room, above the antique chair. Keeping windows and doors closed helps the house warm up; you may also use the solid-fuel stove. On warm days, opening doors and windows creates an effective through-draught.'],
  ['car-charging','Car charging','⚡','Please let us know if you would like to use the onsite car charger. It can be unlocked for €20 for a full charge. Overnight charging is preferred, as our electricity rate is lower after 11pm.'],
  ['entertainment','Entertainment','◉','There are three televisions, with their matching remotes in each room. The sitting-room Fire Stick uses its own small remote with a blue button. The downstairs bedroom has an HDMI cable for gaming devices and the bunk room has an ethernet connection at the desk. Please use the Guest account when streaming. The kitchen has Vappeby and Nattbad Bluetooth speakers, plus a Google Home speaker. Board games and crafts are in the cupboard next to the fridge; playing cards are in the large coffee table in the lounge. The lounge also has MagnaTiles and material craft / wool in the green cabinets. Please take time to return these items to where you found them.'],
  ['instructionvideos','Useful videos','▶','Short, practical videos for waste management, the smart lock, washer dryer, Sage Combi Oven, air fryer, Monsieur Cuisine Smart, hot tub and superking blinds.'],
  ['pantry','Pantry','▣','You are very welcome to use any food items you find in the house. Kindly replace anything you finish, or nearly finish, please.'],
  ['dining','Dining','⌂','The table is set for four. Extra seating includes the wicker bench by the front door, folding chairs behind the kitchen door and outdoor dining chairs. TV-dinner and laptop trays are in the sitting room. Mats and tablecloths are on the kitchen under-counter shelves, and extra table linen is in the square coffee-table drawer.'],
  ['appliances','Appliances','⌘','The iron and steamer are under the hall table; the ironing board hangs on the coat rail. Manuals for the washer dryer, Sage Combi Oven, Air Fryer and Monsieur Cuisine Smart are kept beside or beneath each appliance. The toaster’s left side must be used first when toasting one or two items.'],
  ['towels','Towels','≈','Shower and bath towels are in the hot press / airing cupboard on the upstairs landing. Please do not use these in the hot tub; use the colourful beach towels beside the fridge instead.'],
  ['hot-tub','Hot tub','♨','Enter the code, unclip both clips, lift the front half of the lid onto the back half, then use the bar to raise it vertically. Always supervise children and set the temperature to no more than 37°C for them. No food, glass, fake tan, makeup, sand or pets. Shower after the sea, and always close and clip the lid when not in use.'],
  ['house-rules','House rules','♥','Please eat and drink downstairs; keep glass and breakables away from bare feet outdoors; no smoking indoors, parties, events or unapproved guests; and please keep noise considerate in this family neighbourhood. Return furniture, covers, games and toys as you found them, and do not park on the grass.'],
  ['pets','Pets','♧','Pets must be listed on the reservation. Please clean up after them and do not allow them on the hot tub, beds or couches. Please do not use house towels for pets, and take care they do not damage the house or furniture.'],
  ['check-out','Check out','✓','Check out any time before 2pm. Start the dishwasher, take waste to the recycling area, check the garden for cigarette butts or pet waste, close and clip the hot-tub lid, strip used beds, leave used towels and linen in the bath, and lock all doors and windows. Please report any damage and let Julianne know you have departed.'],
  ['leaving-checklist','Leaving checklist','☑','Before leaving, check streaming accounts are signed out, and look for chargers, devices, clothes, swimwear, toys, baby items and fridge/freezer food. Please make sure all windows are closed and doors locked. Lost property is held for a month, then donated or recycled.'],
  ['damages','Damages & breakages','!','We understand that accidents happen. Please let us know promptly if anything needs to be replaced before the next guests arrive. Fair charges may apply to repair or replace damaged items.'],
  ['review-feedback','Review & feedback','★','Reviews help our family business grow. If anything is not right during your stay, please tell Julianne straight away so she has the chance to fix it. If you enjoyed your stay, we would be very grateful for a Google review.'],
  ['comeback','Come back soon','↗','We hope you will want to return soon. Direct bookings receive the best rates and the same cancellation policies you are used to. Text or call Julianne on 0868215176 to plan another stay.']
];
